From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:38:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] build_features: indicate the SCS and MSCS handling

A program that configures hostapd cannot tell whether the build handles
SCS and MSCS requests, which a build of CONFIG_ROBUST_AV before that
handling does not. Answer "robust-av-scs" in has_feature(), so that
`hostapd -vrobust-av-scs` tells it.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/utils/build_features.h
+++ b/src/utils/build_features.h
@@ -76,6 +76,8 @@ static inline int has_feature(const char
 #ifdef CONFIG_ROBUST_AV
 	if (!strcmp(feat, "robust-av"))
 		return 1;
+	if (!strcmp(feat, "robust-av-scs"))
+		return 1;
 #endif
 	return 0;
 }
